    "video_file_id": "BAACAgIAAyEFAAMBClOLWAACBjBrAXD8e36m10zpbbDkMfbMvEJ_IAACErAAA6eoS6s71AR1-OoJPQQ",
    "video_file_size": 331148,
    "caption": "🔍 Google Gives Web Agents Modern Guidance\n\nThe Modern Web Guidance skill gives coding agents access to about 200 guides on current web development. It targets a familiar problem: Claude Code, Codex, and similar tools still use outdated approaches when browsers support simpler solutions.\n\nThe guidance covers modern frontend work, from markup and styles to browser performance and accessibility. For popups, it points agents to the built-in Popover API instead of complex JavaScript, and recommends CSS Container Queries for responsive layouts.\n\nVersion 1.0 can scan existing code for outdated patterns and propose an upgrade plan. It checks browser compatibility and should preserve required workarounds. Install it with npx modern-web-guidance@latest install.\n\n📊@tech",
