    ],
    "caption": "🌎 US Targets Remote GPU Access\n\nA new US Commerce Department rule requires a re-export license for advanced chips sent to Brazil, Singapore, Indonesia, Malaysia, or Thailand. Data centers there must run KYC checks and monitor links to embargoed countries.\n\nThe rule targets a loophole. Chinese customers could not legally buy advanced GPUs, but could rent remote access through third-country data centers. The source names Megaspeed, whose Malaysia and Indonesia sites served Chinese clients including Alibaba.\n\nRemote access through those hubs had remained legal while direct purchases were blocked. It will now require US approval, making the data centers gatekeepers.\n\n📊@tech",
