    "video_file_id": "BAACAgIAAyEFAAMBClOLWAACBjxrAXD8bk4lWtAWpL_x3IqoMUSUAwACNqAAAll34Evu0hBbEhKnYj0E",
    "video_file_size": 3221601,
    "caption": "🍏 iPhone Duo Gets Basic Face Unlock\n\nIn the second beta of iOS 27.3, Apple added Unlock with Front Camera to the $2000 folding iPhone Duo. It uses the regular front camera, not the TrueDepth hardware behind Face ID, and is currently limited to developers and beta testers.\n\nIt can unlock only the lock screen. The feature cannot open apps or show passwords. Apple Pay still requires Touch ID. After 45 minutes without use, it switches off.\n\nApple warns that the method is less secure than Touch ID or Face ID. It does not work on the inner display, likely because the under-display camera has low resolution.\n\n📊@tech",
