    "video_file_id": "BAACAgIAAyEFAAMBClOLWAACBj5rAXD8h2i5HwpY1kLrp69GBJGy1AACHqsAAhdE8UsYMlwpudbWWj0E",
    "video_file_size": 10116890,
    "caption": "🎮 AI Makes Old Games Look Real\n\nA clip of Assetto Corsa, a 2014 racing simulator, can take a few seconds to identify as gameplay. Modern graphics tools, including NVIDIA DLSS, improve image quality and performance, while advanced shaders and lighting push the result closer to real footage.\n\nAI does not have to generate every frame from scratch. It can enhance conventionally rendered graphics by restoring detail or raising resolution, without rebuilding the whole scene. \n\nGTA 6 is now releasing worldwide, while Rockstar says generative AI was not used to create its game world. Future AAA projects are likely to use AI across development. The stated horizon is 5-10 years of more realistic games.\n\n📊@tech",
